 health  service becomes too much this winter  then vaccine passports and masks may  return  donna all right redmond shannon in  london thank you  a couple in southern india didn't let  flash flooding ruin their wedding day  they found a way to adapt the bride and  groom sailed to the ceremony sitting in  this big metal cooking pot they floated  to the temple through muddy water two  men steering the way some members of the  family apparently swam other use others  used another pot to get there  the couple dry and hopefully living  happily ever after  meet calgary's new mayor ahead a  one-on-one with jody gondeck about her  historic election win  calgary made headlines in 2010 when it  elected the first muslim mayor of a  major north american city and now it's  done it again electing the first female  mayor in the city's history jyoti gandek  is of punjabi heritage and so is the new  mayor of edmonton amrajeet sohi if this  doesn't finally obliterate national  stereotypes of alberta as some kind of  racist backwater writes calgary herald  columnist dawn braid perhaps nothing  ever will well with me from calgary is  jody gondeck mayor-elect  first let me say congratulations to you  thank you so much  can you reflect a bit on your victory  what was it do you think about you and  your campaign the appeal to calgarians  well i think we offered people something  to vote for my campaign team and i have  been very clear from the beginning that  there must be a vision that's  communicated to calgarians and i think  the people of calgary embraced it they  wanted to hear more about what we would  do for resiliency in this city and they  demonstrated that they liked what they  heard by coming out to vote  you have a phd in urban sociology i've  read you've worked as an academic why  did you decide to make the leap to  public office and run for mayor did  something happen that made you say this  is it i'm running  you know it's been an interesting  journey falling in love with this  concept of city building  it started many years ago when i picked  up a couple of projects my dad had left  unfinished when he passed away quite  unfortunately in 2003.  and as i dug in to do some of that work  with his friends and colleagues i  realized that  there was a calling for me in public  service and i did a lot of volunteer  roles in and around the city and my  communities and in 2017 i looked back at  what i had been trying to do to  influence from the outside and i thought  maybe it was time to get a seat at the  table i felt well prepared at that time  and now with four years of counsel under  my belt i feel incredibly well prepared  to serve calgarians as their mayor  i know premier jason kenney has  congratulated you are you ideologically  aligned in any way and what sort of  relationship do you hope to have with  him  i think the greatest alignment that our  city and the provincial government could  have is one where we realize that we all  serve the same people so if we can count  on their assistance in providing the  supports that people need with public  health with child care access to housing  then we can help be that economic engine  again that carries us forward you know i  talked to nahad nenshi last month about  the toxic political atmosphere these  days how hostile and vicious some people  can be how much does that concern you  and and how do you think you'll push  back against it  it is quite concerning and i think a lot  of people who ran as candidates for the  first time in this election  realized just how ugly it can be but i  have a lot of faith that  we have a brighter future ahead i think  people are incredibly optimistic about  it and i think people have realized that  we need to band together to make sure  we're stamping out the voices that try  to be louder than ours  all right jyoti gondek mayor elect of  calgary thanks so much  thanks for having me on  up next rumblings from the red planet  what those sounds mean for exploration  on mars  a remarkable find off the coast of  israel a diver on a weekend treasure  hunt discovered this a sword experts  believe is roughly 900 years old dating  back to the crusades it's about a meter  long and was exposed when sands shifted  in the shallow water of a cove known for  sheltering ships the sword believed to  be made of iron will be x-rayed and  cleaned and maybe reveal clues about the  crusader who once carried it from an eye  on the distant past to an ear on the  distant present the first photograph  ever taken on the surface of mars was  beamed back to earth 45 years ago and  now sounds from the red planet captured  by nasa's perseverance rover are giving  scientists a deeper understanding of  what it's like to roam around up there  mike trolley explains  if your car made a racket like this  you'd get it checked out but nasa named  its mars rover perseverance not  rolls-royce  so all that clanking and scratching  they could care less yeah it's it's not  engineered for you know comfort  so there's definitely sounds of you know  moving up and down it's got a lot of  metal so there's going to be creaking  and groaning a little bit nasa has now  had a few months to study the hours of  sounds first recorded by the rover the  first audio ever captured on another  planet it's not as sexy as the lander's  descent or the subsequent drone flight  but hearing the winds of mars  adds to our sensory feel of another  world it doesn't really tie into the  search for life or anything like that  but it tells us that there were things  that we had predicted about the  atmosphere that we didn't quite get  right nasa scientists knew the martian  atmosphere was thin so they expected  high pitched sounds would either  disappear or appear muffled for example  this is what birds sound like on earth  and to be clear they haven't found birds  on mars but if they did this is what  you'd hear  what surprised them was how far sound  travels on the red planet the mars  helicopter was 80 meters away  yet the rover's microphones were still  able to pick it up proving science  doesn't just look cool with all of our  upcoming uh missions to you know  jupiter's moons different planets around  the solar system i think it would be a  nice um you know soundtrack you know  sounds of the solar system and here i  thought we already had that  [Music]  mike global news toronto  and that is global national for this  tuesday i'm donna friesen tonight's york  canada is near the village of packingham  ontario west of ottawa we'd love to see  your canada please email it to viewers  at globalnational.com  thanks for watching hope to see you here  again tomorrow take care of yourselves  bye-bye  [Music]
 

